# Stata temp/swap files
*.stswp
~*
*.log
*.smcl

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Data files stay in Box, not git
*.dta

# Box Drive sync tombstones, left behind when a file is deleted on the synced drive
*0000000000*

# Python bytecode caches. A .pyc was tracked, so a diagnostic's compiled form showed
# up as a code change on every run that imported it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The scratch rebuild verify_pipeline.py writes to compare the crosswalk against a fresh
# build. Regenerated on every run and never read by anything else -- committing it would
# put a second copy of the crosswalk in the repo, which is the ambiguity the comparison
# exists to remove. outputs/tables/build_manifest.json IS committed: it is the reference
# the comparison is made against.
outputs/temp/_verify_rebuild/

# Retired external inputs, kept only so a past question can be re-answered without
# re-sourcing them. Large, externally sourced and re-downloadable, so the bytes stay out
# of git and reference/archive/README.md carries the provenance instead. The README is
# tracked; the data is not.
reference/archive/*
!reference/archive/README.md

# The sandbox 06_cpi_panel.do writes to so its output can be diffed against the published
# CSVs without overwriting them. Regenerated on demand; committing it would put a second
# copy of the CPI panel in the repo, which is the ambiguity the comparison exists to remove.
outputs/temp/_cpi_port/

# Variant builds from an experiment, e.g. 90_diagnostics/measure_anchor_keying.do, which
# sets ${build_name} so the whole build goes to its own subtree instead of overwriting
# the published one. Regenerated on demand and diffed against master_rename_build; there
# is no reason to keep a second full build in the repo.
outputs/anchor_*/
